Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||03-16-2000||01:36 AM||||A long time (ok, about 4 years. heh) ago I learned a valuable lesson about keeping my mouth shut.. I rarely speak out about an issue unless it's to provide support to a friend or to give info that might help the people involved settle it peacefully or understand the other person's viewpoint.<P>I agree that the person who told these people to leave the forum was out of line.. but I'm not sure that justifies kicking that person off the forum.<P>(small typo here, I accidentally typed justified instead of justifies.. sorry)<P>*everybody* has disagreements with people at one point or another, and if I freaked out on everyone who ticked me off or insulted me, whether personally or business related, I'd make a lot of people mad at me. For example, I was hammering out a contract with a potential client, and when I showed him the invoice for a website (a 70 page site.. took me 2 months to create..), he pulled out an invoice from a competitor (who makes very low quality sites, I've seen them before) and basically said my price was too high. If I didn't need the money so badly, I would have just walked away, but I let him talk my price down by over $300. Personally I found that quite rude, but I didn't say anything.<P>I had 2 people request websites hosted, but some events took place and I found myself unable to afford the server upgrade. These people waited patiently (still are, in fact..) until I got my server upgraded early this month. <P>Hmm.. this post got extremely off-topic.. Basically, I think if people took the time to consider the other person's point of view, a lot of these problems would be solved rather quickly. Instead of jumping in and telling someone they're not welcome, or saying that a person is a poor choice to do business with.. the situation should be worked out by the people involved, and if others do become involved, it shouldn't be name calling and accusations that won't solve anything. I correspond via email with Tom fairly regularly, and I've talked over email with V6pack in the past. I found them both to be very friendly people, as is probably the case in most disputes, and I think this could be resolved without anyone leaving the forum.<P>sorry for the very long post, I didn't intend to say this much when I started typing..<p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 03-16-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000005||Dan86gt3.8||03-16-2000||02:00 AM||||As a maater of fact I think this is a very good topic and should not be deleted.  as to the second person I am not taking sides in the debate between tom and v6pack, the person I am reffering to is an inconsiderate, ________ (you fill it in with whatever you would like) who told 2,yes 2 members to leave.  That is and was what I was reffering to in my post.  I was very concerned that a MEMBER, not an administrator or moderator of the forum told 2 other members to leave the forum and never come back.  This upset me because, one this person had no right, and second we are trying to build a forum with as many fiero enthusiasts as possible, and with hotheads telling people to leave, how can we expect to build a following?  I suggested that instead maybee this person leave, I did not tell him to leave or threaten him.  I was saying "IF". thats all.  I still can't believe that other memebers of the forum would actually condone this behavior from other members, or let it slide and act like the original debate is still the topic, which it is not, this thread is about a rouge meber that told 2 others to leave, plain and simple!  ||||reg||1
