Z||000019||V6pack||03-17-2000||08:02 PM||||Like Motorhead I'm still here too.  I like it here and think Cliff has provided a great resource for us all and has been kind enough to let us express a variety of opinion.  You can't do that everywhere!  <P>I'm toasting you all from my webtv barcalounger work station with a Corona.  And I do mean all of you!<P>I just got my 355 nose and rear scoop from the paint shop and they came out great. So, on this fine Ca. sunny day I say thanks to all for making this hobby a joy and an education and way too much fun to pout over a bump in the road.<P>A special toast to Fierodave and WWT the 3rd for being the folks they are.<BR>V6pack ||||reg||14
Z||000020||sinoloa||03-17-2000||08:35 PM||||I like it here, too!! I don't know what I would do without this forum. Yes, I do. I would've set my Fiero on fire and rolled it down a hill without this forum. When I first got my Fiero, it broke down. We took it to three or four different shops trying to get it fixed since this we are predominantly a Mustang Family.  Several shops refused to even touch the car. They specifically said they 'do not work on Fieros'. One shop even refused to do a complete computer test on it<BR>because the readings were coming up strange. I thought, this isn't UFO technology people. The Fiero People understood that and now my car is running great. In the immortal words of Rodney King, "can't we just all get along!" ||||reg||10
